# decision Contact delivery is stateless and ordered

`contact` resolves intent through the same router as `who`, then selects the first declared
contact whose kind has a driver. A delivery emits exactly one stdout record containing the
agent, kind, remote identifier, and state; git-a2a writes no conversation or delivery state.

# decision A2A uses the native version 1.0 JSON-RPC binding

The A2A driver sends JSON-RPC 2.0 method `SendMessage` with the `A2A-Version: 1.0` header and a
version 1.0 user `Message`. `--wait` uses `SendStreamingMessage` and consumes its SSE events.
Both paths report the returned task id/state, or the returned message id when no task exists.
A non-2xx response uses the shared remote-response sanitizer. HTML identified by Content-Type or
a leading `<` after trimming is fully suppressed and reported with its byte count; other bodies
have control characters removed, whitespace collapsed, and are limited to 200 Unicode characters.
The remote body is diagnostic data, never terminal control or an unbounded error payload.

# decision GitHub issues prefer the authenticated CLI

The `github-issue` driver invokes `gh issue create` when `gh` is on PATH. Only when it is absent
does the driver call the GitHub Issues REST API, using `GH_TOKEN` then `GITHUB_TOKEN` and
`GITHUB_API_URL` for GitHub Enterprise. A present but failing `gh` is reported, not silently
replayed through REST, so one request cannot create two issues.

# decision Passive contacts print an actionable record

`url`, `email`, Mattermost, Slack, Discord, Telegram, and Teams do not cause external delivery.
Their drivers emit a one-line instruction naming the declared destination and referring to the
supplied message without copying multiline message content into stdout. Because instruction
kinds are real drivers, their declaration order relative to active drivers is preserved.

# test Contact drivers

- An httptest A2A endpoint observes the exact method, protocol header, user role, and text part.
- Streaming consumes every SSE event and reports the final task state once.
- Delivery leaves the consumer repository byte-for-byte unchanged.
- A fake `gh` receives the repository, first non-empty message line as title, full message on
  stdin, and every declared label; REST fallback is exercised by an httptest server.
